:"Rep. Goldman, Craig A. [R-TX-12]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"S001226","fullName":"Rep. Salinas, Andrea [D-OR-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OR"},{"bioguideId":"E000071","fullName":"Rep. Ellzey, Jake [R-TX-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-18T14:13:27+00:00","id":"hconres4-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-28","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-28","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"laws":[],"number":"4","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Taxation","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"L000585","district":16,"fullName":"Rep. LaHood, Darin [R-IL-16]","party":"R","state":"IL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-28","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p>This concurrent resolution expresses the sense of Congress that tax-exempt fraternal benefit societies serve as a private economic and social support system,&nbsp;providing benefits to their members&nbsp;is necessary to support the charitable and fraternal activities of the volunteer chapters,&nbsp;and their work should continue to be promoted.</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-03T15:35:39Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Expressing the sense of Congress that tax-exempt fraternal benefit societies have historically provided and continue to provide critical benefits to the people and communities of the United States.","type":"hconres","updateDate":"2026-09-18T08:06:54Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-18T08:06:54Z"}
